-(2) **Candour on caps.** The OpenCode 20-second retrospective token limiter is **not** a strict per-request hard cap: a single in-flight request (with continuations, retries and counter lag) can exceed a nominal reservation. Where a provider or gateway enforces a verifiable per-request limit, use it. Do not claim a mathematical hard cap on one request. Enforceable *operating-budget ceilings* and bounded concurrency are the real safety control.
