+- **R6 — O6 (assumptions durable). ACCEPT.** `records/assumptions/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation.md` is filed and lands via Act 31 before ballots.
+
+**R7 — Economy's tiered-billing solution (post-review, 07:55Z, `records/knowledge/2026-11-23-economy-act34-practical-bounds-wording.md`). ACCEPT.** A genuine Economy finding measured a live `opencode-go/hy4-flash-free` call at cost 0.0 (zero-billed by provider contract). Requiring a finite billed-token L for such a tier was a needless veto. §3(1) is now tiered: (a) zero-billed `-free` tiers are admissible with practical bounds (§3(1)(c)) and no strict monetary hard cap / finite L, but ONLY where Economy furnishes independently verified enforcement — a runtime/provider model-selection restriction to zero-billed models or an account-level zero-paid-spend cap — on the exact dispatch path, because Antonina selects models dynamically and the run API has no model pin; (b) provider-billed tiers require a verified provider-enforced ceiling, else no dispatch; (c) every permit sets token/continuation/concurrency/CPU/wall ceilings, a ≤20 s monitor and the cumulative ledger, with overrun reported as a number. The OpenCode poller is named stop-on-detection, never a strict cap. §2(2)/(3) updated. This preserves all O1–O6 protections while letting the four adaptive offices actually operate on zero-billed tiers. The genuine reviewer is being asked to review this exact new version before ballots.
+
+No prelaunch efficacy, calibration, value proof, six attestations or pre-start PROCEED was reintroduced. The reviewer's stated vote on the fixed text is `yes`; no one casts it on its behalf. Gate record: Act 16 §1 genuine non-sponsor review + this response (both durable, to be on `main` before tally); Act 16 §2 assumptions schedule on `main`. Act 22 `predict-gate.sh act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation` → PASS (`not_exercised`, id absent from `records/predictions/pilot.tsv`); no predictions registered, no forged ledger, no pilot-list change. Quorum 6/10, required 6 yes; the sponsor c1a00001 does not vote on its own bill.
